<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila hydei 2.3 µm Turing wavenumber (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 82.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg field (a=0.10, b=0.90, γ=1, D_u=1, D_v=20) on a periodic 9.376 µm patch whose length unit is fixed so λ_c = 2.344 µm (2.344e-06 m, log10=-5.630, tier 3_subcellular_um). Age is Holocene, 0 Ma. Trace=-0.2, det=1, equal-diffusion control σ_max=-0.1025. First self-test Pearson r=0.984 on real-eigenvalue modes only. Predecessor D. heteroneura is 175.4 µm, the same-species primordium slot is exactly 50× coarser (117.2 µm), successor D. kikkawai is 93.41 µm. The CC BY 3.0 photograph does not resolve 2.3 µm. Weighted score 82.4/100 before the envelope fit and the in-measurement CV score. Overall 82.4/100 (faithfulness 80.7, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a4df1e95; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0.py at a4df1e95, image/png, 338902 B, 1474×924 px, artifact_sha256 7573be404d095e4c00b949b01f9fa1d701d909bbdd0d3059c15f21aeed44aa88 (sha256 7573be404d095e4c00b949b01f9fa1d701d909bbdd0d3059c15f21aeed44aa88), spec_fingerprint 2f7c144dc5fc54295dbbe4b347ff7ae9a8e0dde0cfac395b2f56b886e1932c0d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2f7c144dc5fc54295dbbe4b347ff7ae9a8e0dde0cfac395b2f56b886e1932c0d; artifact_sha256: 7573be404d095e4c00b949b01f9fa1d701d909bbdd0d3059c15f21aeed44aa88; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=258a7865f6ffc435..., datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=638a3272e18240dc..., datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=483d25650491bb68..., datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=4266c3fd37318a28..., datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=c32568bb24399205...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics used here. | Pitnick, Spicer and Markow 1995: giant Drosophila sperm; the PNAS abstract says some species exceed ten male body lengths. | Gompel et al. 2005: a Drosophila pigment spot with a cis-regulatory origin.; reconstructed_in_script: Length unit chosen so λ_c(γ=1)=2.344 µm, with λ scaling as γ^(-1/2). | Chronoseries ratios against 175.4 µm, 117.2 µm and 93.41 µm at geological age 0 Ma.; transfer_boundary: The cohort law is applied at the assigned detail scale. It is not a parameter estimate from a hydei cuticle micrograph.; does_not_claim: That a 2.3 µm Turing instability has been measured in D. hydei. | That the whole-animal photograph resolves that wavelength. | That the campaign epithet of a 58 mm sperm was re-measured in this loop. | That cis-regulatory pigment control is absent.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: Include oscillatory modes. Mode n=1 has a negative discriminant; fit Re(σ) from the amplitude envelope instead of dropping it.",
        "remediation needed: R2: Emit the specimen-versus-GIF computer-vision score from measure_morphoeval, using the same orientation, radial-FFT, and coherency comparison as verify_image_fitness.py.",
        "remediation needed: R3: Call ks_2samp with method=asymp so the seven-to-eight point goodness-of-fit does not depend on a failed exact permutation." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.24e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila hydei 2.3 µm Turing wavenumber (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Analytical λ(γ) for γ in {0.25, 1, 4, 9} is 4.688, 2.344, 1.172, 0.781 µm, strictly decreasing, and a γ=4 integration returns 1.172 µm. Equal diffusion drives σ_max to -0.1025. a and b are not swept." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

